A||N||14||Formula88||Woo Hoo - Feels so good at 100+!||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||10-28-2001||04:28 PM||||Well, I've had my Formula since January, but with clutch, tires, etc. I've never had the time or opportunity to really get her out and stretch her legs.  But that changed today!  After washing her at the local spray wash, I jumped on 540 at the dead end (loop under contruction - last few miles to the end of the loop are pretty deserted) to "blow dry" my car.  There's a early 90's or so Prelude Si in front of me.  No biggie - I just cruise on past him at about 80mph.  Then he decides I must be racing him, so he comes back past me.  Oh, I don't think so!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">  So, I drop it into 4th at about 80 and let her rip.  I blow back past him doing about 95 or so (he never got very far in front of me) and just stayed in it, cuz it felt OH SO GOOD!   So, I see my exit coming up in about a mile and stay in it winding it up to about 5300rpm-5500rpm in 4th gear.  I'm doing about 110mph or so when I let up and coast over into the exit lane.  Into the brakes and she glides to a contented stop at the top of the exit ramp (Prelude going past the exit about the time I stop).   Check mirror - check left - check right.  No cops in sight.  Engine purring like a freshly raced box of kittens.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   I just ease out the clutch and cruise on back home.  Man that felt GOOD!  That's the fastes I've had my Fiero so far.  She was still pulling strong, and I had another gear to go.  Wonder what she'd have pulled in 5th?  Oh, and the headlights never popped up.  Car did start to feel a bit light, but nothing dangerous.  Definately needs the hood vents for stability, though.  My 72 Trans Am could run about 140mph and was rock solid because of the air dams and fender vents.  It worked quite well.<P>Just thought I'd share.  Not really a kill story - the Prelude was just an incidental casualty.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>BTW:  88 Formula 5-speed.  All original, no mods unless you count my RAM clutch and removed intake water diverter as mods.  120K miles, driven daily.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-28-2001||06:35 PM||||I gave Lisa a little ride on the way to Dayton fri nite. Took her to 125, but the wind was really moving it around, really windy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-28-2001||10:49 PM||||That wind will make you pucker at those speeds, huh?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||mrfiero||10-28-2001||10:59 PM||||Why didn't you shift into 5th?  You would have reached 120 MPH easily and wouldn't have had the engine so wound up.  <P>At any rate......a few months ago I was coming back to Denver from southern California in my 5-sp. T-Top '88 GT (with new tires & alignment) and decided to let it all hang out on the last mountain before hitting the plains on I-70.  There are about 3 or 4 good miles with a few nice twisties where you can get going VERY fast (going downhill adds MPH!).  I had the needle buried and it was still pulling by the time I hit flat ground and it was as smooth as can be.....no front end lift or vibrations.  It felt good!<P>I think everyone should "air out" their Fieros every now and then (as long as the conditions warrant it).  <P>Next time use 5th!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||10-28-2001||11:02 PM||||Actually, if I was going to stay in it, I was just about to shift, but my exit was coming up, so I backed out.  I usually shift between 5500 and 6000.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||10-28-2001||11:14 PM||||Ha, funny story, because I can relate.  The other day I was on my way home from work cruising along at my usual 85-90 (love the Alabama freeways) and an Integra pulled out of the slow lane and clipped up behind me.  I never have gotten my car above 90, so I figured, "What the hey, let's do it." So I downshifted and gave the air-starved 2.8 a go.  We stuck together to about 105(now in fifth gear), and I could tell I wasn't even testing him.  He had a lot more than me, but it was fun regardless.  We kept at about 105, hit a tiny bit of traffic but weaved through it, and we were starting to approach my exit.  I kept on it, and got to about 115 pulling a long slow curve towards town.  He backed off before we hit the curve, not like we were racing, but it was nice to know I was having more fun than him <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  So pulled off the highway, downshift and using the brakes, everything felt solid.  The car idled nicely as I sat at the light, with him right behind me.  I was giggling like a little school girl, but he was acting all macho behind me as if nothing had happened.  I think it was fun....can't wait till my car is where I want it to be!  I wonder how low I can cut my daily drive time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||10-28-2001||11:38 PM||||Fieros are pretty fun in high speeds. I remember when I had my 88 coupe. Right after I installed my beautiful 16 inch wheels with Kumho tires. I was up in Toronto for a weekend. Anyway, I somehow forgot I had work at 11 am sunday morning. So basicly I got onto the highway and hauled ass down to the Falls. I basicly had my foot to the floor the entire time, I had the speedo burried for like 20 mins. It was pointing at the 10mph mark for miles and miles. I had almost no traffic in my way at all, so it was great. I had my new 16 inch tires humming, quite the break in for them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Felt really good haveing my duke runing at 4300 rpm and having my speedo peged for that long a time. Car was completely stable, headlights keept down, car was tracking fine, felt responsive.<P>Best of all I didnt pass any cops taking raydar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">. That would have really screwed up my day. Oh and I made it in time to work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol||||reg||14
Z||000007||Cooter||10-29-2001||12:05 AM||||I took the GT up to just over 100 a couple of times while making the g-tech runs. Unfortunately, I can't shift into 5th  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Nashco- give me a call and I will let you drive my car with the 3.4/4 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||12:42 AM||||Just don't be cheap on tires, know what they are, that they're at the right psi, and what they are rated at.  A blowout at 60 mph can be deady, one at 100+ leaves little doubt.  Not to mention the fiero thatll be in little bits.  And be glad you don't have a factory speed limiter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||GTMike||10-29-2001||02:28 AM||||i drive at 100+ mph  all the time. i have been doing some work out at my dads house in wellingtong colorado and i live in ft collins.   there is a strech of about 10 miles of I 25  and i zip up there 3 times a week, the the hole way at around 105.  and if i'm feeling frisky   i take her up to a little past 120. its fun.  i hope when i get my 3.4  i'll be able to get to 100mph alot faster<P>------------------<BR>87GT mostly stock, cold air intake, no cat. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtmike1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||10-29-2001||02:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>I took the GT up to just over 100 a couple of times while making the g-tech runs. Unfortunately, I can't shift into 5th   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Nashco- give me a call and I will let you drive my car with the 3.4/4 speed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>LOL..is this a trick?  I see some sort of Austin Powers scene coming on...beautiful women with guns in their jumblees, ready to take me out!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rick 88||10-29-2001||09:48 AM||||Formula 88,<P>I have a a 72 Trans Am also. It is a stock Lucerne Blue 455-HO. Turbo 400 with 3.08 posi.I've never had the guts to top end it but it loafs at 100 mph and is very stable.<BR>An efficient hood vent would defintely help out on my 88 GT at speed. I already have a spare hood, I'm just trying to decide on a vent style.<P>Rick 88||||reg||4
Z||000012||Formula88||10-29-2001||09:58 AM||||Very cool, Rick!  I'd love to see pics of your TA.  Mine was white, auto, with either the 3.23 or 3.42 rear end.  It would hit about 140, but ran out of rpms long before it ran outta guts.  No telling what it would have run with an overdrive!  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Gerald||10-29-2001||05:38 PM||||I was so shocked this weekend. My little 4 banger Fiero hit 120 mph. All ive done for mods is taken out the water separater. I even have low compression on cyl 2. I was so proud. Now the car is gonna get a 3.8 sc over winter. Then Ill take it to a track instead of highway 2.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
